{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 RCA (rebar-debug): CONFIRMED DEFECT. MCP 1.29.0 defines generic `mcp.server.fastmcp.server.Settings` before `FastMCP` under postponed annotations, so `Settings.model_fields[\"lifespan\"]` remains `_complete=False` with `ForwardRef(\"Callable[[FastMCP[LifespanResultT]], AbstractAsyncContextManager[LifespanResultT]] | None\")`. The module never rebuilds the model after `FastMCP` becomes available. On the first `FastMCP()` construction, pydantic-settings 2.15 `DefaultSettingsSource` inspects that incomplete field and emits `IncompleteFieldDefinitionWarning`; with the warning promoted to error, public `build_server()` aborts at `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:627` before construction completes.\n\nDiscriminating proof: (1) direct upstream-only `FastMCP(\"direct\")` reproduces in a fresh process without importing rebar, ruling out rebar config/tool/schema and Starlette integration; (2) fresh-process state is model=False/field=False before construction, first construction emits exactly one warning and auto-completes the model, second construction emits zero; (3) pre-calling public Pydantic `Settings.model_rebuild()` returns True, resolves the annotation, and makes the first construction warning-free; (4) holding MCP 1.29.0/Pydantic 2.13.4 fixed, both pydantic-settings 2.14.2 and 2.15.0 begin with the same unresolved model, while only 2.15 warns—commit 57d192544c exposed a pre-existing MCP defect rather than creating it; (5) untreated-success versus pre-rebuilt rebar construction produced identical host/port/lifespan values, identical default lifespan context `{}`, 61 tools, and identical serialized tool-schema SHA-256 b516757c10ab635d84b3b6345f7096973e25f0dc598c5e7b58bee935661ca70e. Upstream modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk#3294 confirms the exact v1 defect and endorses `Settings.model_rebuild()` after import as the one-line workaround; v1 is critical-fixes-only.\n\nDefect legitimacy: pydantic-settings sources/utils.py:32-53 defines incomplete FieldInfo as unsafe for settings-source inspection and warns it may silently fail to resolve values; rebar supports MCP 1.x and publishes `rebar-mcp`. Caller-dependency gate: expected post-fix is only complete Settings metadata plus no warning before first rebar server construction. `build_server()` callers consume the returned FastMCP server; no caller inspects or depends on the warning/incomplete metadata, and runtime/schema/lifecycle parity is proven above. Direct upstream FastMCP consumers outside rebar’s factory are unaffected. Safe to enter Phase 2 with a local constructor-boundary compatibility rebuild; no dependency, lifecycle, startup, tool, or schema behavior change."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786917548745887001,"uuid":"db21eca2-8332-447f-b435-607cc910ef24"}